{
  "id": 321131401,
  "iid": 16844,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan/dissectors/packet-ieee1722.c: Fixed the ieee1722 fdf_rvals table ranges",
  "description": "I noticed while debugging AVTP traffic that the IEEE 1722 dissector had the wrong ranges set in the \"fdf_rvals\" table. The original values assumed that the values for that field included an additional 3 bits at the end that were assumed to be masked to 0, but in reality the values did not include these 3 bits, so the ranges in this table should be smaller and lower.\n\nThis bug was causing the stream format to always show as \"AM824\".\n\nSource for the information relating to this can be found in IEC standard 61883-6 Table 16 \"Subformat and FDF allocations\":\n\n![Screenshot 2024-08-13 at 2.39.10 PM.png](/uploads/2fe3919e51f6ce91d5eebe4847c39794/Screenshot_2024-08-13_at_2.39.10_PM.png)\n\n**Original (incorrect) value:**\n\n![Screenshot 2024-08-13 at 2.36.56 PM.png](/uploads/d40b9a53a11afb64b10e2c252968fe7d/Screenshot_2024-08-13_at_2.36.56_PM.png){width=1751 height=423}**Fixed value:**\n\n![Screenshot 2024-08-13 at 2.54.00 PM.png](/uploads/7f555bd2689523de3357cf7402babb98/Screenshot_2024-08-13_at_2.54.00_PM.png){width=658 height=334}",
